1
00:00:03,940 --> 00:00:08,980
YAMU YAMU YAMU YAMU!

2
00:01:03,140 --> 00:01:06,905
Any fool could have seen that
Noah never planned to set us free.

3
00:01:08,320 --> 00:01:13,180
He claimed that doorway led back to the
real world, but it was just another trap.

4
00:01:13,980 --> 00:01:16,597
Now it's time to go
straight to the source and

5
00:01:16,680 --> 00:01:19,327
take down the man behind
all of this madness.

6
00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:21,760
My stepfather, Gozoboro.

7
00:01:22,760 --> 00:01:25,817
If he thinks his ridiculous
plan to drag the entire

8
00:01:25,900 --> 00:01:28,517
world into this digital
dump is going to succeed,

9
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:30,960
then he's more senile than I thought.

10
00:01:32,540 --> 00:01:35,893
I'm sure that old fool is
sitting in my office right now.

11
00:01:36,260 --> 00:01:38,180
I've taken him down once before,

12
00:01:38,480 --> 00:01:41,774
and I'm planning to do it
again, but this time for good.

13
00:01:44,180 --> 00:01:47,380
That scrawny little dwerp
double-crossed us again.

14
00:01:47,700 --> 00:01:49,797
I knew we shouldn't have trusted him.

15
00:01:49,880 --> 00:01:51,900
Now he's toast. Wait, Joey.

16
00:01:52,160 --> 00:01:54,777
We have to come up with
a plan that makes sense.

17
00:01:54,860 --> 00:01:57,297
Yeah, and I already came up with a plan.

18
00:01:57,380 --> 00:02:00,760
We shake Noah upside down
till he tells us the way out.

19
00:02:00,920 --> 00:02:03,577
I'm gonna have to agree
with Joey on this one, guys.

20
00:02:03,660 --> 00:02:05,680
Only Noah knows where the exit is.

21
00:02:05,880 --> 00:02:07,645
And we're running out of time.

22
00:02:07,760 --> 00:02:10,878
Because pretty soon, the
whole world will be trapped.

23
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:13,557
I guess I shouldn't have trusted Noah.

24
00:02:13,640 --> 00:02:15,900
This is all my fault. Not true.

25
00:02:17,060 --> 00:02:21,697
You believe there's still good inside of
Noah, and there's nothing wrong with that.

26
00:02:21,780 --> 00:02:23,133
Well, no one else does.

27
00:02:23,240 --> 00:02:24,070
Give them time.

28
00:02:24,153 --> 00:02:27,924
After everything he's done, it's
hard to believe he could change.

29
00:02:28,260 --> 00:02:30,620
Goodbye, boys. Seto!

30
00:02:31,820 --> 00:02:32,650
No!

31
00:02:33,140 --> 00:02:35,120
What have you done? Oh, no!

32
00:02:35,460 --> 00:02:37,695
That kid made us sniff at a dude, too!

33
00:02:38,220 --> 00:02:39,050
Serenity.

34
00:02:41,220 --> 00:02:42,050
Eww!

35
00:02:48,780 --> 00:02:52,137
Noah's acts of rage are fueled
by an anger deep inside,

36
00:02:52,220 --> 00:02:55,960
But we can help him see the
light. I hope so. And soon.

37
00:02:57,220 --> 00:02:58,050
All right.

38
00:02:58,133 --> 00:02:59,857
Let's go find Noah and
figure out how to get

39
00:02:59,940 --> 00:03:02,437
out of here so we can
stop Gozoburo's plan.

40
00:03:02,520 --> 00:03:03,740
But how?

41
00:03:04,380 --> 00:03:06,262
Once we're free from cyberspace,

42
00:03:06,420 --> 00:03:08,217
we can warn people in the real world that

43
00:03:08,300 --> 00:03:11,580
Gozoburo's planning to
digitize the planet. I hope...

44
00:03:12,200 --> 00:03:13,030
Stop that!

45
00:03:13,520 --> 00:03:14,400
Too late!

46
00:03:15,660 --> 00:03:18,778
Tristan, I couldn't understand
a thing you just said.

47
00:03:19,100 --> 00:03:21,060
You're almost all chimp now.

48
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:25,320
It's Skull Night!

49
00:03:25,600 --> 00:03:27,365
There's a whole bunch of them!

50
00:03:29,320 --> 00:03:30,860
Joey, behind you!

51
00:03:31,200 --> 00:03:33,560
Where are these monsters coming from?

52
00:03:33,920 --> 00:03:35,508
This should keep them busy.

53
00:03:38,020 --> 00:03:39,080
Oh, no!

54
00:03:39,440 --> 00:03:40,400
Oh, yes!

55
00:03:41,260 --> 00:03:42,980
We gotta do something!

56
00:03:43,380 --> 00:03:45,909
Last I checked, running
away was something.

57
00:03:46,080 --> 00:03:47,315
But we're surrounded!

58
00:03:47,680 --> 00:03:49,460
There's no way out!

59
00:03:54,200 --> 00:03:55,030
Serenity!

60
00:03:55,120 --> 00:03:55,950
Serenity!

61
00:03:56,460 --> 00:03:57,290
Stop!

62
00:03:59,220 --> 00:04:00,200
Joey, no!

63
00:04:01,060 --> 00:04:02,360
This better work.

64
00:04:02,520 --> 00:04:03,638
It's our only hope.

65
00:04:03,900 --> 00:04:05,580
Come forth, Curse of Dragon!

66
00:04:08,320 --> 00:04:09,880
Dragon Flame attack!

67
00:04:13,840 --> 00:04:15,080
Alright, Yu-Gi!

68
00:04:15,240 --> 00:04:16,360
It's my turn now.

69
00:04:16,540 --> 00:04:18,540
I play my Axe Raider!

70
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:25,880
It's good to be back in
the real world again.

71
00:04:26,340 --> 00:04:28,480
Mokuba's body was a perfect fit.

72
00:04:28,740 --> 00:04:33,034
Now I can move ahead with my plan and
stop my father from completing his.

73
00:04:33,660 --> 00:04:34,860
Access confirmed.

74
00:04:35,300 --> 00:04:36,888
Welcome to Central Command.

75
00:04:37,800 --> 00:04:39,320
It's so simple.

76
00:04:39,640 --> 00:04:44,520
I'll destroy the central computer that
allows my father's virtual world to exist,

77
00:04:44,900 --> 00:04:47,740
thus destroying every
mind that's trapped there.

78
00:04:47,900 --> 00:04:51,317
My father's, Seto's, and
all of Yugi's friends.

79
00:04:51,400 --> 00:04:52,720
Those fools,

80
00:04:52,960 --> 00:04:54,537
thinking I was actually going to help them

81
00:04:54,620 --> 00:04:57,326
escape was the last
mistake they'll ever make.

82
00:04:57,760 --> 00:04:59,100
Now it's time.

83
00:04:59,440 --> 00:05:00,860
The past is over.

84
00:05:01,500 --> 00:05:04,840
And I'll take my father
down with his own satellite.

85
00:05:05,900 --> 00:05:07,980
Initiating satellite reprogramming.

86
00:05:08,340 --> 00:05:09,575
Preparing for attack.

87
00:05:15,040 --> 00:05:19,160
I'll put an end to my stepfather's
nonsense once and for all.

88
00:05:20,940 --> 00:05:22,660
Don't you know how to knock?

89
00:05:22,860 --> 00:05:25,840
I guess you never taught
me manners. Have a seat.

90
00:05:26,040 --> 00:05:28,158
It's time for a father and son chat.

91
00:05:28,700 --> 00:05:30,060
In your dreams.

92
00:05:30,280 --> 00:05:31,900
Seto, just give in now.

93
00:05:32,120 --> 00:05:34,337
You'll make things much
easier on yourself,

94
00:05:34,420 --> 00:05:39,100
or you can choose to meet the same fate
as your little friends. Take a look.

95
00:05:40,260 --> 00:05:43,260
My army of monsters is
about to wipe them out.

96
00:05:49,160 --> 00:05:51,537
Your little threats don't scare me at all.

97
00:05:51,620 --> 00:05:54,738
So why don't you let us go
before I really get angry?

98
00:05:56,340 --> 00:05:58,300
You haven't changed a bit.

99
00:05:59,280 --> 00:06:00,110
All right.

100
00:06:00,240 --> 00:06:03,017
I know the perfect way to
settle our differences.

101
00:06:03,100 --> 00:06:06,420
Do you recall the chess match
we had the day I met you?

102
00:06:06,700 --> 00:06:08,680
Well, I propose a rematch.

103
00:06:10,700 --> 00:06:12,780
You are not worth my time.

104
00:06:13,120 --> 00:06:15,197
Why would I want to play
chess against someone

105
00:06:15,280 --> 00:06:18,104
who couldn't even beat
me when I was just a kid?

106
00:06:19,300 --> 00:06:24,200
What makes you think I'm talking about you
and I playing another chess game, Seto?

107
00:06:25,040 --> 00:06:27,700
Then what did you have in mind, Gozaburo?

108
00:06:28,140 --> 00:06:29,240
Take a guess.

109
00:06:29,460 --> 00:06:31,620
It's a game you're quite fond of.

110
00:06:32,020 --> 00:06:33,160
Duel Monsters!

111
00:06:33,800 --> 00:06:34,630
Really?

112
00:06:34,720 --> 00:06:36,160
What are you up to?

113
00:06:36,520 --> 00:06:37,540
You seem mad.

114
00:06:37,740 --> 00:06:42,197
I thought you'd jump at the chance to
duel your stepfather to win your freedom.

115
00:06:42,280 --> 00:06:44,080
You thought wrong, Gozaburo.

116
00:06:44,440 --> 00:06:47,037
You can't play with my
life like it's a game.

117
00:06:47,120 --> 00:06:49,473
Well, that's exactly what you did to me,

118
00:06:49,560 --> 00:06:53,780
Seto, on the day you stole
the Kaiba Corporation from me.

119
00:06:54,600 --> 00:06:55,430
How heartbreaking.

120
00:06:55,513 --> 00:07:00,106
You're here because I outsmarted you and
took away your precious little company.

121
00:07:00,500 --> 00:07:03,657
I'm here because the virtual
world gives me limitless power.

122
00:07:03,740 --> 00:07:08,320
Soon I'll use it to digitize the
world, but first I'll get rid of you.

123
00:07:09,300 --> 00:07:12,437
And why do you have to beat
me in a duel to do that?

124
00:07:12,520 --> 00:07:15,180
To humiliate you, like you humiliated me.

125
00:07:15,500 --> 00:07:17,637
And once I beat you at your favorite game,

126
00:07:17,720 --> 00:07:20,397
I'll make sure you never
stand in my way again.

127
00:07:20,480 --> 00:07:23,620
I'll erase your mind and
reprogram you as my servant.

128
00:07:23,920 --> 00:07:27,802
Then you'll obey my every command
just like the rest of the world.

129
00:07:28,440 --> 00:07:31,260
I have never served anyone but myself,

130
00:07:31,480 --> 00:07:35,068
and I've never backed down from
a challenge either, Gozoboro.

131
00:07:35,200 --> 00:07:36,600
So let's duel.

132
00:07:37,280 --> 00:07:40,339
The satellite's almost
reprogrammed for destruction.

133
00:07:45,980 --> 00:07:47,700
I'll find you, Pharaoh!

134
00:07:51,480 --> 00:07:54,240
Even if that means
shutting this place down!

135
00:07:56,680 --> 00:07:57,510
Warning!

136
00:07:57,780 --> 00:07:59,380
Main power is offline!

137
00:07:59,760 --> 00:08:01,400
Main power is offline!

138
00:08:02,200 --> 00:08:03,030
No!

139
00:08:03,113 --> 00:08:04,360
I was almost finished!

140
00:08:05,980 --> 00:08:08,000
Releasing magnetic dock! Hey!

141
00:08:08,400 --> 00:08:10,047
We're no longer locked down!

142
00:08:10,520 --> 00:08:11,350
Excellent.

143
00:08:11,440 --> 00:08:14,440
Now we have to find the
other passengers. Merrick.

144
00:08:15,900 --> 00:08:19,040
Are you prepared to
humiliate yourself, Seto?

145
00:08:19,620 --> 00:08:20,800
You tell me.

146
00:08:21,040 --> 00:08:22,099
Let's get started.

147
00:08:22,900 --> 00:08:25,100
Now then, I'll go first.

148
00:08:25,660 --> 00:08:28,660
And you criticized me
for having no manners?

149
00:08:28,980 --> 00:08:30,627
Go ahead and make your move.

150
00:08:30,840 --> 00:08:32,400
I play Painful Choice.

151
00:08:32,660 --> 00:08:35,777
It's a magic card that allows
me to take any five cards.

152
00:08:35,860 --> 00:08:37,978
I know what the card does, you fool.

153
00:08:38,820 --> 00:08:43,114
First you show me any five cards from
your deck, then I pick one of them.

154
00:08:43,340 --> 00:08:46,977
That card goes into your hand,
the others head to the graveyard.

155
00:08:47,060 --> 00:08:49,480
Now, show me your five cards already.

156
00:08:50,540 --> 00:08:55,240
Well, someone's feeling a bit anxious,
so feast your eyes on my cards.

157
00:08:55,700 --> 00:08:58,935
I have a strong feeling you've
encountered them before.

158
00:08:59,400 --> 00:09:00,560
Take a close look.

159
00:09:00,820 --> 00:09:03,320
Do these five cards seem familiar to you?

160
00:09:04,700 --> 00:09:05,860
It can't be.

161
00:09:06,040 --> 00:09:07,240
Not those cards.

162
00:09:07,880 --> 00:09:11,360
It's the five pieces of
Exodia, the Forbidden One!

163
00:09:14,200 --> 00:09:18,120
Yes, I have all five pieces
of Exodia in my deck.

164
00:09:18,320 --> 00:09:20,720
But not for long. Trust me.

165
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:22,600
We'll see about that, Seto.

166
00:09:22,760 --> 00:09:24,037
After all, we've just begun.

167
00:09:24,120 --> 00:09:27,700
And I know all about your
painful history with Exodia.

168
00:09:30,980 --> 00:09:31,810
Exodia!

169
00:09:31,893 --> 00:09:32,960
It's not possible!

170
00:09:34,940 --> 00:09:36,180
Exodia, obliterate!

171
00:09:43,680 --> 00:09:47,777
your point that's
history besides i'm about

172
00:09:47,860 --> 00:09:50,760
to send four pieces of
exodia to the graveyard

173
00:09:52,380 --> 00:09:56,857
then what are you waiting for any
duelist holding all five pieces of

174
00:09:56,940 --> 00:10:01,077
exodia automatically wins but since
he drew them using a painful choice

175
00:10:01,160 --> 00:10:05,517
magic card i can send four of them
to the graveyard Didn't I teach you

176
00:10:05,600 --> 00:10:09,237
that hesitation is a form of weakness
when basing down your enemies,

177
00:10:09,320 --> 00:10:10,150
Seto?

178
00:10:11,760 --> 00:10:13,417
He must be up to something.

179
00:10:13,500 --> 00:10:16,637
Even he's not dumb enough to
throw away his best cards.

180
00:10:16,720 --> 00:10:18,500
I'll let you keep that one.

181
00:10:18,820 --> 00:10:22,820
Then the right arm of Exodia goes
to my hand and the others go away.

182
00:10:23,960 --> 00:10:27,860
Now I'll place one monster in
defense mode and end my turn.

183
00:10:28,360 --> 00:10:29,240
For now.

184
00:10:29,680 --> 00:10:32,977
But it won't be long before
you hear me say checkmate.

185
00:10:33,060 --> 00:10:34,040
Stand back.

186
00:10:34,260 --> 00:10:35,260
It's my move now.

187
00:10:36,340 --> 00:10:39,040
Emergency backup generators activated.

188
00:10:39,640 --> 00:10:41,464
All systems operating normally.

189
00:10:42,320 --> 00:10:43,900
Good. Where was I?

190
00:10:45,040 --> 00:10:47,140
Once that satellite attacks,

191
00:10:47,380 --> 00:10:52,260
the entire virtual world will instantly
shut down along with every mind inside.

192
00:10:53,640 --> 00:10:55,740
An uninvited guest.

193
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:57,540
It's not like it matters.

194
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:01,020
This place is history.

195
00:11:02,400 --> 00:11:04,580
30 minutes to satellite attack.

196
00:11:07,140 --> 00:11:08,260
The coast is clear.

197
00:11:08,440 --> 00:11:09,270
Let's go.

198
00:11:10,900 --> 00:11:11,900
Come on, Joey.

199
00:11:12,440 --> 00:11:14,264
Are those monsters coming back?

200
00:11:14,520 --> 00:11:15,717
Don't worry, Serenity.

201
00:11:15,800 --> 00:11:17,741
It seems like we're safe for now.

202
00:11:18,740 --> 00:11:20,000
Or maybe not.

203
00:11:20,540 --> 00:11:22,364
Looks like our work's not done.

204
00:11:22,500 --> 00:11:23,330
All right.

205
00:11:23,413 --> 00:11:24,592
Let's do our thing, you.

206
00:11:27,620 --> 00:11:29,697
25 minutes to satellite attack.

207
00:11:29,780 --> 00:11:31,840
Evacuate virtual simulators.

208
00:11:34,580 --> 00:11:36,800
I must find those fools.

209
00:11:38,540 --> 00:11:39,520
What's this?

210
00:11:40,080 --> 00:11:42,620
Satellite set to destroy central computer.

211
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:48,320
23 minutes to satellite attack.

212
00:11:48,520 --> 00:11:50,240
This is it. Right, Father?

213
00:11:50,460 --> 00:11:52,695
You're finally giving Kaivocorp to me.

214
00:11:52,960 --> 00:11:54,840
You had your chance, Noah.

215
00:11:56,160 --> 00:11:58,420
He's lied to me for the last time.

216
00:12:09,680 --> 00:12:13,140
It's time to make my escape
and leave those fools behind

217
00:12:15,560 --> 00:12:19,477
My father said he's bringing the
whole world in here And that means

218
00:12:19,560 --> 00:12:24,800
I'll never have to be alone again
We'll be one big happy family

219
00:12:28,060 --> 00:12:29,140
Noah, stop!

220
00:12:30,020 --> 00:12:32,057
You've got to get a hold of yourself.

221
00:12:32,140 --> 00:12:35,669
You're in danger, too, and we
all have to work together now.

222
00:12:36,520 --> 00:12:37,780
Moki, you're right.

223
00:12:38,480 --> 00:12:39,520
Mokuba's a fool.

224
00:12:39,940 --> 00:12:44,469
I just remembered, you can't escape with
us to the real world without a body.

225
00:12:44,560 --> 00:12:47,420
But I bet Seto can make you a body.

226
00:12:47,680 --> 00:12:49,940
I mean, you're our family, Noah.

227
00:12:51,640 --> 00:12:54,000
Why can't I stop thinking about this?

228
00:12:54,220 --> 00:12:57,279
I mean, after all, Noah,
we are brothers, aren't we?

229
00:12:58,160 --> 00:12:59,340
He trusts me.

230
00:12:59,780 --> 00:13:01,140
After all I did.

231
00:13:07,500 --> 00:13:10,560
Brotherhood, family, who needs it?

232
00:13:11,920 --> 00:13:13,500
Hmm, that's behind me.

233
00:13:14,020 --> 00:13:16,880
Soon my so-called family
will be gone for good.

234
00:13:17,140 --> 00:13:19,140
21 minutes to satellite attack.

235
00:13:19,360 --> 00:13:21,000
Evacuate virtual simulator.

236
00:13:21,120 --> 00:13:22,220
What have I done?

237
00:13:24,400 --> 00:13:25,480
Oh, no.

238
00:13:28,740 --> 00:13:30,620
Lackluster Soldier, attack!

239
00:13:33,920 --> 00:13:36,040
Now, go X-Raider!

240
00:13:39,420 --> 00:13:41,740
18 minutes to satellite attack.

241
00:13:44,880 --> 00:13:46,740
My brother believes in me.

242
00:13:46,960 --> 00:13:48,195
I can't let him down.

243
00:13:48,500 --> 00:13:50,265
I have to stop that satellite.

244
00:13:51,120 --> 00:13:51,950
Whoa!

245
00:13:52,280 --> 00:13:53,110
The controls!

246
00:13:53,480 --> 00:13:54,892
I can't stop the attack!

247
00:13:55,620 --> 00:13:56,450
No!

248
00:13:56,660 --> 00:13:58,577
That intruder must have done all this!

249
00:13:58,660 --> 00:14:00,537
Now Mokuba and the others are doomed!

250
00:14:00,620 --> 00:14:01,637
It's all my fault!

251
00:14:01,720 --> 00:14:03,544
15 minutes to satellite attack.

252
00:14:03,980 --> 00:14:05,215
Evacuate immediately.

253
00:14:07,280 --> 00:14:11,820
I place one card face down and
summon Force Raider in attack mode!

254
00:14:15,100 --> 00:14:17,380
He has a monster in defense mode.

255
00:14:17,660 --> 00:14:20,097
It could be more powerful
than my Force Raider.

256
00:14:20,180 --> 00:14:23,480
But then again, knowing
Go Zaburo, he's bluffing.

257
00:14:24,400 --> 00:14:25,871
Force Raider, attack now!

258
00:14:25,980 --> 00:14:27,880
Destroy his face down, monster!

259
00:14:33,180 --> 00:14:34,010
What?

